Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; BAUER GROUP Header Authenticator - remove the enterprise policy (Windows).
;
; Removing the ID from ExtensionInstallForcelist is enough on its own: Chrome
; uninstalls a previously force-installed extension when it leaves that list.
; Apply, then RESTART the browser and confirm on chrome://extensions.
;
; If it survives the restart (a known Chromium bug, most often on macOS), escalate
; with uninstall-force-windows.reg and then re-apply THIS file to lift the block it
; leaves behind.
;
; This file is also step 2 of the escalation path, which is why it clears
; ExtensionSettings rather than only the forcelist entry.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; READ BEFORE APPLYING - two values here are SHARED with other extensions:
;
;   ExtensionInstallForcelist is a numbered list. This file deletes value "1",
;   which is the slot force-install-windows.reg writes. If your fleet force-installs
;   anything else, check the numbering first (reg query, see below) and delete only
;   the slot holding jncjhkagdjiiohjfmbpmlemdchbkjaib.
;
;   ExtensionSettings is ONE REG_SZ holding JSON for EVERY managed extension. This
;   file deletes the whole value. If other extensions are configured there, do NOT
;   apply that part - edit the JSON and drop only the
;   "jncjhkagdjiiohjfmbpmlemdchbkjaib" object instead.
;
; Inspect first:
;   reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\ExtensionInstallForcelist"
;   reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome" /v ExtensionSettings
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

; --- Google Chrome ---
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\ExtensionInstallForcelist]
"1"=-

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome]
"ExtensionSettings"=-

; Managed configuration (domains + secrets pushed by policy). Keyed by extension
; ID, so deleting the whole subtree touches nothing else.
[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\3rdparty\extensions\jncjhkagdjiiohjfmbpmlemdchbkjaib]

; --- Brave ---
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\BraveSoftware\Brave\ExtensionInstallForcelist]
"1"=-

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\BraveSoftware\Brave]
"ExtensionSettings"=-

[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\BraveSoftware\Brave\3rdparty\extensions\jncjhkagdjiiohjfmbpmlemdchbkjaib]

; --- Microsoft Edge ---
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\ExtensionInstallForcelist]
"1"=-

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge]
"ExtensionSettings"=-

[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\3rdparty\extensions\jncjhkagdjiiohjfmbpmlemdchbkjaib]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The secret is NOT revoked by uninstalling. Device-local secrets go with the
; extension, but anything synced lives in the user's browser account, and a copy
; may sit in any export the user made. Decommissioning a protected service means
; ROTATING THE SECRET on the server. Treat this file as removing an access path,
; never as revoking access.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
